### Works with the IntelliJ HTTP client or the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
@gw = http://localhost:8080

### Catalogue
GET {{gw}}/api/products

### Stock levels
GET {{gw}}/api/inventory

### 1) Happy path -> CONFIRMED
POST {{gw}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerEmail": "asha@example.com",
  "items": [ { "skuCode": "IPHONE-15", "quantity": 1 }, { "skuCode": "USB-C-CABLE", "quantity": 2 } ] }

### 2) Not enough stock (only 5 MacBooks) -> CANCELLED by inventory
POST {{gw}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerEmail": "ravi@example.com", "items": [ { "skuCode": "MACBOOK-AIR", "quantity": 10 } ] }

### 3) Payment declined (> 1,50,000) -> CANCELLED + stock released (compensation)
POST {{gw}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerEmail": "meera@example.com", "items": [ { "skuCode": "MACBOOK-AIR", "quantity": 2 } ] }

### 4) Unknown product -> 400 (not retried, doesn't trip the circuit breaker)
POST {{gw}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerEmail": "x@example.com", "items": [ { "skuCode": "DOES-NOT-EXIST", "quantity": 1 } ] }

### Watch the saga (paste an id from above)
GET {{gw}}/api/orders

### Payments
GET {{gw}}/api/payments

### "Emails" sent
GET {{gw}}/api/notifications
